# App versioning

TaskMesh uses SemVer `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` in root `package.json`, mirrored in `src/lib/appVersion.ts` (`APP_VERSION_CREATED_AT`) and `client/src/lib/appVersion.ts` (`APP_VERSION` + `APP_VERSION_CREATED_AT`).

**MAJOR stays `0`** until an explicit breaking public API / incompatible data migration (ask the user if unclear).

## Historical baseline (T0076)

As of T0076, MINOR was set from the number of Drizzle SQL migrations on disk (`drizzle/*.sql`): **22 files** (`0000_init` … `0021_default_theme`). This Task itself is a non-schema enhancement, so PATCH is **1** → **`0.22.1`**.

That catch-up applies **once**. From this merge onward, **do not re-count migrations**. Increment from the current `package.json` version using the table below on **each finished Task** (Issue or Enhancement), including `/worktask` and ad-hoc `phase-*` work.

**T0142 milestone:** `0.50.0` is the 0.5 Beta cut (a jump from `0.47.7`, not a single MINOR +1). GitHub Release `v0.50.0-beta` is a pre-release. That publish resets working `RELEASE_NOTES.md` to the stub. Later finish-ups increment from the current `package.json` and prepend a notes block as usual (recreate the stub first if the file is empty).

## When to bump (finish-up only)

Bump **once** when the user asks to **finish up** (the commit that merges to `main`), not on every WIP commit. QA-only follow-ups on the same unreleased branch do not get an extra bump.

Every finished Task that ships to `main` must bump **exactly one** of MINOR or PATCH (or, rarely, MAJOR):

| Change | Bump |
|--------|------|
| Feature that **changes DB schema** (new Drizzle migration file(s) in this work) | **MINOR** +1, reset PATCH to `0` |
| Feature enhancement or issue/bug fix **without** a new migration | **PATCH** +1 |
| Breaking public API / incompatible data migration | **MAJOR** +1, reset MINOR and PATCH to `0` (rare; ask if unclear) |

Schema-changing work is MINOR only — do not also increment PATCH. Multiple new SQL files in one Task still count as **one** MINOR bump for that finish-up.

## Fields to update together

1. Root `package.json` `version` (and the matching `version` entries at the top of `package-lock.json`)
2. `APP_VERSION_CREATED_AT` in `src/lib/appVersion.ts` — UTC ISO datetime of this finish-up merge to `main` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ`)
3. `APP_VERSION` and `APP_VERSION_CREATED_AT` in `client/src/lib/appVersion.ts` (same strings)

Do **not** set `releasedAt` in git. Finish-up does not deploy and does not stamp `releasedAt`. On a production host, `deploy/deploy-prod.sh` still writes `data/prod-release.json` after that host’s health checks succeed. The API exposes `releasedAt` only when that sidecar’s `version` matches the running `package.json` version. This development host does not write that file on finish-up. A leftover `data/prod-release.json` from an earlier local deploy still reports `releasedAt` until the file is removed.

## Workflows and skills

- [development-rules.mdc](development-rules.mdc) finish-up step 1 **must** bump version (or confirm this branch already has the bump) **and** update [`RELEASE_NOTES.md`](../../RELEASE_NOTES.md) in that same commit (recreate the stub if the file was cleared after a GitHub release publish). When the Task adds major user-facing functionality, also update [`FEATURES.md`](../../FEATURES.md) in that commit.
- [/worktask](../skills/worktask/SKILL.md) finish-up **must** do the same bump + release-notes update (and `FEATURES.md` when applicable) in the feature-branch finish-up commit (before the PR merges), and mention the new version in the completion comment.

## API / UI

JSON under `/api` includes `meta: { version, createdAt, releasedAt }`. `releasedAt` is `null` until an Administrator deploys this version on a production host. The shell shows `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (e.g. `v0.22.1`).
